==Serbo-Croatian==
{{wikipedia|lang=sh}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/bêoɡrad/|lang=sh}}
* {{hyphenation|Be|o|grad}}
* {{audio|Sr-beograd.ogg|audio}}

===Etymology===
Composed of [[Ekavian]] Serbo-Croatian {{term|beo|bȅo|white|lang=sh}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{recons|bělъ|lang=sla-pro}}) and {{term|grad|grȃd|city|lang=sh}} (from {{etyl|sla-pro|sh}} {{recons|gordъ|lang=sla-pro}}). The city is named after the white wall of the fortress that enclosed the city. See also {{term|Biograd|lang=sh}}, {{term|Белгород|Бе́лгород|tr=Bélgorod|sc=Cyrl|lang=ru}}, {{term|Białogard}}.

